Write a solution to find the number of times each student attended each exam.
Return the result table ordered by student_id and subject_name.


SOLUTION:

SELECT 
    Students.student_id,
    Students.student_name,
    Subjects.subject_name,
    COALESCE(COUNT(Examinations.subject_name), 0) AS attended_exams -- counts the amount of each subject test they attended
FROM Students 
CROSS JOIN Subjects -- gets each subject for each student
LEFT JOIN Examinations -- gets exam data without losing information on those who didn't take a certain test
    ON Students.student_id = Examinations.student_id 
    AND Subjects.subject_name = Examinations.subject_name
GROUP BY Students.student_id, Subjects.subject_name -- summing over individual students and subjects
ORDER BY student_id, subject_name;
